          {
            title: 'Put',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Put is a trick-taking card game that involves tricks, trump, following suit. The game originated in Europe and has become popular worldwide.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Country/Region of Origin: England\nTime Period: Sixteenth to nineteenth century\nHistorical Development: Put was played in England from the sixteenth to the nineteenth century; rules recorded by Willughby (1672) and Cotton (1674); related to Truc (France/Spain) and Truco (South America).\nCultural Significance: English tavern game of the period; popular in servants' quarters with loo, whist, all fours.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
